From 7d524c1a933a0b8bd98bf8ba3948f54924b179fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:42:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Rewrite pages.terratern.com root to serve the linktree
 page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lets the CMS keep living here (Marketing CRM sidebar) while the
public-facing domain still points at just the linktree page: any
request to pages.terratern.com/ is rewritten (not redirected — the
URL bar still shows pages.terratern.com) to /linktree.html.

Two manual steps in Vercel still needed for this to take effect:
1. Remove pages.terratern.com from the terratern-ads-landing-page
   project's Domains settings (a domain can only be attached to one
   Vercel project at a time).
2. Add pages.terratern.com to this project's (smartping-email)
   Domains settings instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LHzxqv9S6k47oG19wZF3Kx
---
 vercel.json | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vercel.json b/vercel.json
index c29018c..9b6b051 100644
--- a/vercel.json
+++ b/vercel.json
@@ -1,4 +1,11 @@
 {
+  "rewrites": [
+    {
+      "source": "/",
+      "has": [{ "type": "host", "value": "pages.terratern.com" }],
+      "destination": "/linktree.html"
+    }
+  ],
   "functions": {
     "pages/api/cron-simple.js": {
       "maxDuration": 300
-- 
2.43.0


